WHAT THIS COVERS
  STANDARD.md, README.md, CONTRIBUTING.md, everything under profiles/, and the
  "description" text carried inside the JSON Schema documents under
  src/tcat_standard/schema/.

WHAT IT DOES NOT COVER
  The Python source under src/tcat_standard/ (excluding schema/), which is MIT
  licensed -- see LICENSE.

WHY TWO LICENSES
  The DMSP for this project sets MIT as the default for research software and
  CC-BY-4.0 for documentation, tutorials, and example workflows. The schema
  documents sit on that boundary: they are machine-readable, but their content is
  documentation -- normative prose about what a valid dataset is. Licensing them
  CC-BY-4.0 is what lets the standard be quoted, adapted, and profiled by other
  groups, which is the point of publishing a standard at all.

  The synthetic example data under examples/ is also CC-BY-4.0.

